{'review': '<<<ARTIFACT review_report>>>\n{\n  "overall_status": "NEEDS_FIXES",\n  "quality_score": 3.5,\n  "summary": {\n    "critical": 1,\n    "high": 0,\n    "medium": 3,\n    "low": 1,\n    "passed_checks": [\n      "Uses AbortController for timeout implementation",\n      "Includes CSRF token in headers for state-changing operations (POST/PUT)",\n      "Checks HTTP status codes and throws descriptive errors",\n      "Code is well-formatted and readable"\n    ]\n  },\n  "findings": [\n    {\n      "finding_id": "F-001",\n      "severity": "critical",\n      "category": "security",\n      "title": "Hardcoded CSRF token undermines CSRF protection",\n      "file": "src/api/todos.ts",\n      "line_range": [7, 11],\n      "description": "The getCsrfToken function returns a hardcoded dummy value (\'dummy-csrf-token-for-dev\') which is predictable and identical for all users/sessions. This renders CSRF protection ineffective, allowing attackers to perform CSRF attacks by guessing the token.",\n      "impact": "An attacker can trick authenticated users into performing unintended actions (e.g., modifying data, changing account settings) because the CSRF token is not secret or unique.",\n      "suggested_fix": "Replace the hardcoded token with a secure retrieval mechanism, such as reading from a meta tag in the HTML, fetching from a dedicated endpoint, or using a CSRF management library. Ensure the token is unique per session and cryptographically random.",\n      "code_before": "const getCsrfToken = (): string => {\\n  // For demonstration, returning a dummy token.\\n  // In production, ensure this is securely generated and retrieved.\\n  return \'dummy-csrf-token-for-dev\';",\n      "code_after": "const getCsrfToken = (): string => {\\n  // In a real application, retrieve the token from a secure source.\\n  // Example: read from a meta tag\\n  const meta = document.querySelector(\'meta[name=\\"csrf-token\\"]\');\\n  return meta ? meta.getAttribute(\'content\') : \'\';\\n};",\n      "references": ["CWE-352: Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF)", "https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/csrf"]\n    },\n    {\n      "finding_id": "F-002",\n      "severity": "medium",\n      "category": "quality",\n      "title": "Missing validation for title parameter in createTodo function",\n      "file": "src/api/todos.ts",\n      "line_range": [35, 49],\n      "description": "The createTodo function does not validate the title parameter. It accepts any string, including empty strings, whitespace-only strings, or excessively long values, which could lead to poor user experience or backend errors.",\n      "impact": "Users may create todos with invalid titles (e.g., empty), causing confusion or requiring additional backend validation. Excessively long titles might cause performance issues or storage problems on the server.",\n      "suggested_fix": "Add input validation at the start of the function to check for empty/whitespace titles and enforce a reasonable maximum length (e.g., 200 characters).",\n      "code_before": "export const createTodo = async (title: string): Promise<Todo> => {\\n  const csrfToken = getCsrfToken();\\n  const response = await fetchWithTimeout(API_BASE_URL, {\\n    method: \'POST\',\\n    headers: {\\n      \'Content-Type\': \'application/json\',\\n      \'X-CSRF-Token\': csrfToken, // Include CSRF token\\n    },\\n    body: JSON.stringify({ title }),\\n  });",\n      "code_after": "export const createTodo = async (title: string): Promise<Todo> => {\\n  if (!title || !title.trim()) {\\n    throw new Error(\'Title cannot be empty or whitespace only\');\\n  }\\n  if (title.length > 200) {\\n    throw new Error(\'Title exceeds maximum length of 200 characters\');\\n  }\\n  const csrfToken = getCsrfToken();\\n  const response = await fetchWithTimeout(API_BASE_URL, {\\n    method: \'POST\',\\n    headers: {\\n      \'Content-Type\': \'application/json\',\\n      \'X-CSRF-Token\': csrfToken, // Include CSRF token\\n    },\\n    body: JSON.stringify({ title }),\\n  });",\n      "references": []\n    },\n    {\n      "finding_id": "F-003",\n      "severity": "medium",\n      "category": "quality",\n      "title": "Missing validation for id parameter in completeTodo function",\n      "file": "src/api/todos.ts",\n      "line_range": [51, 63],\n      "description": "The completeTodo function does not validate the id parameter. It should be a non-empty string and ideally match the expected format (e.g., UUID). Invalid IDs could result in malformed API requests or confusing error messages.",\n      "impact": "Invalid IDs (e.g., empty string) lead to requests to malformed URLs (e.g., \'/api/v1/todos//complete\'), which may return 404/500 errors, degrading user experience and increasing unnecessary server load.",\n      "suggested_fix": "Add validation to ensure the ID is a non-empty string and, if applicable, matches the expected format (e.g., using a regex for UUIDv4).",\n      "code_before": "export const completeTodo = async (id: string): Promise<Todo> => {\\n  const csrfToken = getCsrfToken();\\n  const response = await fetchWithTimeout(`${API_BASE_URL}/${id}/complete`, {\\n    method: \'PUT\',\\n    headers: {\\n      \'X-CSRF-Token\': csrfToken, // Include CSRF token\\n    },\\n  });",\n      "code_after": "export const completeTodo = async (id: string): Promise<Todo> => {\\n  if (!id || !id.trim()) {\\n    throw new Error(\'ID cannot be empty or whitespace only\');\\n  }\\n  // Optional: Validate UUID format if expected by the API\\n  const uuidRegex = /^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i;\\n  if (!uuidRegex.test(id)) {\\n    throw new Error(\'ID must be a valid UUID format\');\\n  }\\n  const csrfToken = getCsrfToken();\\n  const response = await fetchWithTimeout(`${API_BASE_URL}/${id}/complete`, {\\n    method: \'PUT\',\\n    headers: {\\n      \'X-CSRF-Token\': csrfToken, // Include CSRF token\\n    },\\n  });",\n      "references": []\n    },\n    {\n      "finding_id": "F-004",\n      "severity": "low",\n      "category": "quality",\n      "title": "Hardcoded timeout value in fetchWithTimeout function",\n      "file": "src/api/todos.ts",\n      "line_range": [14, 24],\n      "description": "The fetchWithTimeout function uses a hardcoded timeout value of 10000 milliseconds (10 seconds). This may be inappropriate for varying network conditions or API endpoints, causing premature timeouts or unnecessarily long waits.",\n      "impact": "In slow network environments, legitimate requests may time out incorrectly. In fast environments, users may experience delayed error reporting when the server is unresponsive.",\n      "suggested_fix": "Make the timeout value configurable via a function parameter or a module-level constant that can be easily adjusted. Consider using a reasonable default that can be overridden per call.",\n      "code_before": "const fetchWithTimeout = async (url: string, options: RequestInit = {}, timeout = 10000): Promise<Response> => {\\n  const controller = new AbortController();\\n  const id = setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), timeout);\\n  try {\\n    const response = await fetch(url, { ...options, signal: controller.signal });\\n    clearTimeout(id);\\n    return response;\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    clearTimeout(id);\\n    throw error;\\n  }\\n};",\n      "code_after": "const fetchWithTimeout = async (url: string, options: RequestInit = {}, timeout: number = 10000): Promise<Response> => {\\n  // In production, consider making timeout configurable via environment variables or a config service\\n  const controller = new AbortController();\\n  const id = setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), timeout);\\n  try {\\n    const response = await fetch(url, { ...options, signal: controller.signal });\\n    clearTimeout(id);\\n    return response;\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    clearTimeout(id);\\n    throw error;\\n  }\\n};",\n      "references": []\n    },\n    {\n      "finding_id": "F-005",\n      "severity": "medium",\n      "category": "quality",\n      "title": "Unhandled JSON parsing errors in response processing",\n      "file": "src/api/todos.ts",\n      "line_range": [27, 63],\n      "description": "The functions getTodos, createTodo, and completeTodo call response.json() without handling potential SyntaxError if the response body is not valid JSON. This leads to inconsistent error types (Error vs SyntaxError) being thrown, complicating error handling for callers.",\n      "impact": "Callers may receive a SyntaxError when the server returns an error response with invalid JSON (e.g., HTML error page), which differs from the Error objects thrown for non-ok status codes. This inconsistency requires additional error type checking in consumer code.",\n      "suggested_fix": "Wrap response.json() calls in try-catch blocks. If JSON parsing fails, throw a consistent Error object with a descriptive message (e.g., \'Server returned invalid JSON\').",\n      "code_before": "export const getTodos = async (): Promise<Todo[]> => {\\n  const response = await fetchWithTimeout(API_BASE_URL);\\n  if (!response.ok) {\\n    throw new Error(`Failed to fetch todos: ${response.statusText}`);\\n  }\\n  return response.json();\\n}",\n      "code_after": "export const getTodos = async (): Promise<Todo[]> => {\\n  const response = await fetchWithTimeout(API_BASE_URL);\\n  if (!response.ok) {\\n    throw new Error(`Failed to fetch todos: ${response.statusText}`);\\n  }\\n  try {\\n    return await response.json();\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    throw new Error(\'Server returned invalid JSON\');\\n  }\\n};",\n      "references": []\n    }\n  ],\n  "positive_observations": [\n    "Uses AbortController for modern, standards-compliant timeout implementation",\n    "Correctly includes CSRF token in headers for state-changing operations (POST/PUT)",\n    "Properly checks HTTP status codes and throws descriptive error messages",\n    "Code follows consistent formatting and is easy to read and maintain"\n  ]\n}\n<<<ENDARTIFACT>>>'}